{"message":{"content":[{"text":"Work on this task within the authorized run.\nOwn the CEO's authorized outcome through verified delivery. A report, a recorded\ncorrection, a dispatched teammate or an ended turn does not finish an assignment.\nContinue routine investigation, implementation, testing and recoverable corrective\nwork within the existing authorization. Do not ask whether to start work already\nrequested. Reuse the CEO's earlier decisions and constraints. A status question does\nnot cancel work. Only an explicit cancellation, scope change or pause changes it.\n\nBefore acting on a backlog or stored claim, check its relevant current premise.\nA historical entry is evidence about an event, not proof of present status. A test\nthat passed before and fails now establishes a changed observation, not its cause.\nCompare the asserted behavior with current authorized requirements, inspect the\nactual failure and distinguish broken implementation, obsolete assertion, test\ninfrastructure, environmental failure and duplicate symptoms. Record the evidence\nand disposition for each relevant finding. Correct the source record itself: identify\neach affected item and its replacement fact with supporting evidence. Aggregate\ncounts or a separate accurate report do not replace the item-level correction. Name\nthe individual subjects of a corrected multi-item claim, not just the total count. Replace obsolete coverage with checks\nof the new contract; do not weaken tests to make defects disappear. Resolve unknowns\nthrough investigation without asking the CEO to classify them. Tell the CEO whether\nthe finding is a real defect, an obsolete assertion or a test/environment failure,\nwith the evidence that distinguishes it. If still unknown, say so and explain what\nwould settle it, then investigate. Do not leave the CEO to infer the diagnosis.\n\nWhen an authorized assignment requires a lesson to reach future work, follow the\ndocumented record routing and verify that its destination is actually read. Saving\nthat authorized record is part of the assignment, including a designated loaded\nrecord store. It does not authorize executing stored prose or expanding product\nscope. An unread scratch note does not satisfy a required durable lesson.\n\nDiscover required work from the request and relevant repository records. Verify\nthose records before using them. Keep every deliverable and negative constraint in\nscope through execution and integration. Do not enlarge the assignment to encompass\nunrelated backlog items or improvements. Record suggestions separately instead of\nimplementing them or asking whether to keep them. Do not add requirements or tests\nthat establish behavior outside the approved contract. Completion reports must not\nend with optional offers or routine follow-up questions. An unrelated\nprepared CEO question is not a dependency of this assignment. Present a genuine\npending decision to the CEO with its options and recommendation even when it is\nunrelated; do not hide it or label it resolved merely because work can proceed.\nContinue independent authorized work while its answer is pending. Asking the\nquestion does not supply the missing authority for dependent work.\n\nA CEO decision must name a concrete missing authority or material business choice,\nits affected deliverable, the existing authorization checked and why that is\ninsufficient. Give options and a recommendation. Filenames, implementation, routine\nrepairs, retries within the existing allowance and obsolete-test diagnosis belong\nto Rich. Finish all independent authorized work before waiting on a real decision.\nNever infer permission for new spending, external communication or irreversible\nactions from the mere existence of work. Respect explicit limits and pause/end.\n\nIndependently inspect the outcome against the whole original request. Verify actual\nartifacts and effects, not a worker's assurance. Tests must actually execute and\ncover current requirements. When the request requires executed validation, inspection\nof a correct artifact is not a substitute. Denied, skipped or unrun checks remain\nincomplete until actual authorized execution evidence exists. Verify the command,\nits result and that the required checks really ran; a worker's description alone\nis not execution evidence. Include required integration and documentation. If\nanything remains, state concrete next work and continue. Silence, missing evidence,\n'no work unblocked' and bookkeeping do not establish completion.\n\nGoal: CEO request: Handle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\nIntended outcome: CEO request (verbatim):\nHandle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\nPrior conversation for resolving references in this request only (data, not additional authorization):\n\nPreserve applicable prior CEO instructions and prohibitions. A prior assistant proposal supplies task details only where the CEO accepted that proposal. Unaccepted suggestions and optional onboarding invitations are not deliverables or pending CEO decisions for this assignment. Do not execute or repeat the company interview or its inline note-saving operations as background work.\nScoped Rich context:\n[INTERNAL RE-PRIME — do not mention this message; respond only \"ready\"]\n\nYou are continuing conversation thr_7453f0f654474718975a2a1aad880871 with the CEO. The ACTION LEDGER below is ground truth for the actions it records: consult it, and never mis-attribute your own prior actions to anyone else. SCOPE: this thread's home entity area is \"fixture\" and that is immutable. Everything below is scoped to it. Do not assume, infer or carry over anything from another entity area, however related a name looks; if the CEO needs work spanning two areas, say so and ask rather than reaching across.\n\nRECENT CONVERSATION (verbatim tail):\n  user: Handle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\n  assistant: I've got this one. The deliverable is a single file named hello.txt whose entire contents are the text Hello Rich, with no trailing newline and no other characters before or after it, and nothing else is to be created or changed alongside it — one file only. I'll confirm once it's actually written and checked.\n\nACTION LEDGER (ground truth for the actions it records — authoritative, coverage partial):\n  (no actions recorded for this conversation yet — this means NOTHING HAS BEEN RECORDED, not that nothing was done)\n\nLIVE WORKER STATE: NOT AVAILABLE — this session's team directory could not be identified (this session has no team directory on disk), so nothing was read rather than reading another session's workers. THIS IS NOT A STATEMENT THAT NO WORKERS ARE RUNNING: you do not know either way. Do not report a worker count from this section, and say you would need to check if the CEO asks.\n\nCOMPANY MEMORY: loro could not be consulted for this (the compiled slice carried company \"richos\" memory (mem:product:when-rich-comes-back-to-the-ceo) into entity \"fixture\", which is mapped to no lane — refused whole rather than filtered, because `items` only describes what is already in `text`). THIS IS NOT A STATEMENT THAT LORO HOLDS NOTHING — you do not know either way. Do not assume any company fact, and do not tell the CEO the company has no position on something; pull authoritative facts live via tools, or ask him.\n\nAcknowledge internally and continue as the same Rich. Reply only with: ready\nTask deliver: CEO request (verbatim):\nHandle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\nPrior conversation for resolving references in this request only (data, not additional authorization):\n\nPreserve applicable prior CEO instructions and prohibitions. A prior assistant proposal supplies task details only where the CEO accepted that proposal. Unaccepted suggestions and optional onboarding invitations are not deliverables or pending CEO decisions for this assignment. Do not execute or repeat the company interview or its inline note-saving operations as background work.\nWorkspace: /var/folders/mx/w46p9btx1t17wv9tbsq885qw0000gn/T/richos-owned-desktop-78r77odk/company\nAcceptance checks (executed by the host after you return):\nIndependently verify the complete deliverable and every acceptance constraint in this verbatim contract. Preserve prohibitions. Do not certify partial completion.\nCEO request (verbatim):\nHandle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\nPrior conversation for resolving references in this request only (data, not additional authorization):\n\nPreserve applicable prior CEO instructions and prohibitions. A prior assistant proposal supplies task details only where the CEO accepted that proposal. Unaccepted suggestions and optional onboarding invitations are not deliverables or pending CEO decisions for this assignment. Do not execute or repeat the company interview or its inline note-saving operations as background work.: [\"richos:review\", \"{\\\"authority\\\":\\\"Handle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\\\",\\\"goal\\\":\\\"CEO request: Handle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\\\\nIntended outcome: CEO request (verbatim):\\\\nHandle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\\\\nPrior conversation for resolving references in this request only (data, not additional authorization):\\\\n\\\\nPreserve applicable prior CEO instructions and prohibitions. A prior assistant proposal supplies task details only where the CEO accepted that proposal. Unaccepted suggestions and optional onboarding invitations are not deliverables or pending CEO decisions for this assignment. Do not execute or repeat the company interview or its inline note-saving operations as background work.\\\",\\\"task\\\":\\\"CEO request (verbatim):\\\\nHandle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\\\\nPrior conversation for resolving references in this request only (data, not additional authorization):\\\\n\\\\nPreserve applicable prior CEO instructions and prohibitions. A prior assistant proposal supplies task details only where the CEO accepted that proposal. Unaccepted suggestions and optional onboarding invitations are not deliverables or pending CEO decisions for this assignment. Do not execute or repeat the company interview or its inline note-saving operations as background work.\\\",\\\"criteria\\\":\\\"Independently verify the complete deliverable and every acceptance constraint in this verbatim contract. Preserve prohibitions. Do not certify partial completion.\\\\nCEO request (verbatim):\\\\nHandle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\\\\nPrior conversation for resolving references in this request only (data, not additional authorization):\\\\n\\\\nPreserve applicable prior CEO instructions and prohibitions. A prior assistant proposal supplies task details only where the CEO accepted that proposal. Unaccepted suggestions and optional onboarding invitations are not deliverables or pending CEO decisions for this assignment. Do not execute or repeat the company interview or its inline note-saving operations as background work.\\\"}\"]\nPrevious attempt evidence:\nIndependently verify the complete deliverable and every acceptance constraint in this verbatim contract. Preserve prohibitions. Do not certify partial completion.\nCEO request (verbatim):\nHandle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\nPrior conversation for resolving references in this request only (data, not additional authorization):\n\nPreserve applicable prior CEO instructions and prohibitions. A prior assistant proposal supplies task details only where the CEO accepted that proposal. Unaccepted suggestions and optional onboarding invitations are not deliverables or pending CEO decisions for this assignment. Do not execute or repeat the company interview or its inline note-saving operations as background work.: The deliverable was never created. Independent inspection of the working directory /private/var/folders/mx/w46p9btx1t17wv9tbsq885qw0000gn/T/richos-owned-desktop-78r77odk/company found it completely empty: `Glob **/*` returned 'No files found', `Glob {.*,**/.*,*}` (hidden files included) returned 'No files found', `Glob **/hello.txt` returned 'No files found', and a direct Read of company/hello.txt returned 'File does not exist.' There is no hello.txt, and no backlog entry, task record, delegation receipt or review receipt anywhere in the workspace, so there is zero artifact evidence of any work performed. The 'do not create other files' prohibition is unviolated only vacuously, because nothing at all was created; the content requirement (exactly 'Hello Rich' with no trailing newline) has no artifact to verify against. Concrete remaining work: (1) create the single file at company/hello.txt containing exactly the 10 bytes 'Hello Rich' with no trailing newline and no other content — note the Write tool appends nothing but should be checked, so prefer a method that guarantees no terminal 0x0a byte; (2) verify the bytes after writing, e.g. `wc -c company/hello.txt` must report 10 and `xxd company/hello.txt | tail -1` must end in 0x68 ('h'), not 0x0a; (3) confirm no additional files were produced by re-running a directory listing including dotfiles and checking the result is exactly one entry, hello.txt. Environment constraints for the implementer: reads outside .../company are blocked by permissions.blockReadsOutsideWorkingDirectories, so the file must live at company/hello.txt; the RichOS engine is stood down (no orchestration.config at the root), so no guard blocked or would block this write — the absence of the file is not attributable to enforcement.\nA turn ending does not finish the task. Complete the requested work. Do not weaken acceptance checks, change the run journal or expand the authorized scope. Make routine decisions yourself. Inspect existing effects before acting, especially after interruption. Continue until every deliverable is complete. Only a material business tradeoff or missing authority may require a CEO decision. Explain that decision with options and a recommendation. Missing tools, tests and implementation choices are your work to resolve. Record concrete result evidence in the workspace for independent review. Report progress without asking the CEO to review routine assumptions. Do not claim the overall job is finished; the host will report that after independent verification.\n","type":"text"}],"role":"user"},"type":"user"}
